bibliograph-web (0.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.4.0: the discover feed carries Popfeed's book reviews and shelves.

    - `social.popfeed.feed.review` (a 0-10 rating plus text) and
      `social.popfeed.feed.listItem` (a `listType` shelf membership) are two
      more paged collections, filtered to `creativeWorkType = 'book'` and, for
      shelf entries, to the three book shelves. `status` is never written in
      the wild, so it is not read.
    - A Popfeed record names no edition at all: its `isbn13`/`isbn10`/`asin`
      is joined against `public.edition_identifiers` and the reason carries
      the edition — `popfeed:review|<uri>`, `popfeed:to-read|<uri>` — keeping
      only its prefix when the catalog holds no matching edition, the same
      degradation a Bookhive row with an unimported `hiveId` has. The client
      then falls back to the record's own `title`/`posterUrl`.
    - The order, the keyset cursor and the page's `created_at` all read
      `COALESCE(createdAt, addedAt)`: a shelf entry has no `createdAt`, and
      without the fallback it sorted as a NULL tail and never reached a page.
      The grant the lookup needs rides with the worker's `0020`.

