 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:40:00 +0000

bibliograph-web (0.2.25-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.25: the catalog gains an enumeration read, and the PDS proxy stops
    working past the caller's budget.

    - `net.olamaelcu.livtet.biblio.listEditions` (new, `GET`, edge-served):
      a keyset walk over `editions_pkey` with `cursor` (the last uri of the
      previous page, opaque) and `limit` up to 5 000, returning
      `{items: [{uri, title, indexedAt}], cursor?}`. Nothing else could
      enumerate the catalog: `searchEditions` needs a term and
      `resolveEditions` an identifier, so a crawler had no way in. One page is
      one index scan — 5 000 uris in 180 ms — so 57 pages cover all 282 103
      editions. A malformed cursor restarts at the beginning.
      `community.lexicon.service.describe` lists it; 50 methods now.
    - The PDS proxy bound drops from 15 s to 4 s, under the 5 s a Livtet biblio
      read allows (`REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS`; its catalog health probe allows
      2.5 s). Past that point the edge was reading for a caller that had
      already aborted — during a PDS stall that is how 446 `getRecord`s became
      `499`s at nginx in six hours. A timeout now answers
      `504 UpstreamTimeout` rather than `502 UpstreamUnavailable`, so
      `bibliograph_pds_proxy_requests_total{status="504"}` separates the two;
      any other failed hop stays `502`.
    - Nothing else changes for callers: the forwarded surface, the HappyView
      dependency and the nginx vhost are untouched, and no migration is
      involved.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:30:00 +0000

bibliograph-web (0.2.24-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.24: the two entity resolvers are queries, so nothing about them reads
    as an authenticated write.

    - `net.olamaelcu.livtet.biblio.resolveContributors` and
      `resolvePublishers` were declared `"type": "procedure"` with a JSON body.
      A procedure is an authenticated write in atproto, so every client — and
      the docs page, which tagged them `DPoP` while describing them as
      read-only and anonymous — treated an anonymous catalog read as one that
      needs a DPoP session. The edge never required one (both NSIDs are
      dispatched to `handleEntityGet`, never proxied to HappyView), so the
      declaration was the only thing to fix.
    - Both are now `query` with `parameters`, and their identifier pairs travel
      as repeated `identifiers=issuer:value` parameters
      (`?identifiers=isbn13:9780441478125&identifiers=isni:0000000121032683`).
      Each entry splits on its **first** colon: an issuer never contains one, a
      value may. A pair with no colon, an empty issuer or an empty value is
      `400 InvalidRequest` rather than a silently dropped match, duplicates
      collapse, and the 100-pair cap is unchanged. `offset`/`limit` parse from
      the query string.
    - The POST path is gone, not deprecated: `dispatchPost` no longer has an
      entity branch, the `entityResolve` dependency and `handleEntityResolve`
      are deleted, and `POST` on either NSID is `405 MethodNotAllowed` like
      every other query. `ENTITY_PROCEDURES` was empty afterwards and is
      removed; `ENTITY_METHODS` was a copy of `ENTITY_QUERIES` and is removed
      too. The parsed-pair contract lives in `lib/server/xrpc/identifiers.ts`,
      free of SvelteKit imports so the review of the colon rule is a unit test.
    - `community.lexicon.service.describe` still names 49 methods: the two moved
      between the registries, they did not join or leave the surface. The
      lexicons report 27 queries and 17 procedures now instead of 25 and 19.

