bibliograph-web (0.2.22-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.22-5: every XRPC call is timed, by NSID and by the backend that
    answered it.

    - `bibliograph_xrpc_request_duration_seconds{method, backend, outcome}` is
      recorded around the handler dispatch actually runs, so one series per
      call whichever of `catalog`, `feed`, `happyview` or `pds` served it. The
      HTTP histogram could not answer this: `route` is the id
      `/xrpc/[...method]`, so every NSID shares one series.
    - `bibliograph_upstream_request_duration_seconds{method, upstream,
      outcome}` times the HappyView and PDS hops alone, so `xrpc - upstream` is
      this edge's own cost and `upstream` is what the caller waited on beyond
      it.
    - The NSID allowlist was missing 30 of the 48 methods this deployment
      answers — `getGenresOfBook` and `getIdentifiedFormats` among them — so
      those calls were reported as `method="other"`. It now matches
      `serviceMethods()`, and a test fails when a method is added to the
      surface without being added to the allowlist.

